WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.680
Even without Chadwick Boseman, "Black Panther"&nbsp;
is ready to claw its way back to the top of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.740
box office. Here's everything you should&nbsp;
know before your next trip to Wakanda.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.060
Obviously, Marvel Studios had to drastically&nbsp;
change its plans for "Black Panther:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:17.040
Wakanda Forever" following Chadwick Boseman's&nbsp;
death, and it pushed its original May 6, 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.560
release date to July 8, 2022. Angela Bassett,&nbsp;
Queen Ramonda herself, told Entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.280
Tonight that there had been five drafts of&nbsp;
the script after his passing. She explained,

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:30.120
"I don't know what it's going to look like at all.&nbsp;
There have been about five incarnations of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.380
script and I hear another one's coming. Of course,&nbsp;
with our dear king [Boseman] going on to glory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.460
a lot of things had to be shifted and changed.&nbsp;
[...] Hopefully it will be satisfying, I think,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.880
for the fans and it will be honorable&nbsp;
of our Chad [...] We love our king."

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.720
This all meant that production had to&nbsp;
be pushed back until the summer of 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.100
and it lasted until March 2022. The&nbsp;
film was pushed again to November 11,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:55.140
2022, amongst several other Marvel movies, with&nbsp;
Variety reporting that these delays were due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:59.340
production issues. Thankfully, the film is still&nbsp;
on track to arrive in theaters later this year.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.100
The first "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever" teaser&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.940
is an enlightening look at the sequel without&nbsp;
actually giving too much away. The emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:11.160
footage is scored to Tems' cover of Bob Marley's&nbsp;
"No Woman No Cry," as Wakanda mourns its fallen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:17.040
king. Meanwhile, Shuri, Queen Ramonda, Nakia, and&nbsp;
Okoye all grieve for their loved one. Wakanda is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.180
in a very weak position, so it isn't long before&nbsp;
Namor shows up and starts causing trouble for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:25.620
Shuri and her family. Unfortunately, it isn't&nbsp;
clear why this war has erupted between Wakanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:30.240
and Talocan, but it probably has something to do&nbsp;
with Talocans seeing the water as their realm.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.420
There are brief shots of some kind&nbsp;
of giant research ship lowering two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.320
people in mechanical suits into the ocean, so&nbsp;
perhaps they've trespassed on the Talocans'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.740
territory — or damaged something&nbsp;
which has enraged them. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.580
there are several glimpses of Namor and&nbsp;
the Talocans warring with the Dora Milaje,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:48.540
so let's hope for some thrilling fights&nbsp;
on land and at sea. It's entirely possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.380
that outside forces are manipulating the two&nbsp;
nations, but there's nothing in the trailer to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:57.600
suggest a secret big bad just yet — even if the&nbsp;
internet thinks otherwise. But we'll get to that.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.500
The most important takeaway from the teaser is&nbsp;
that it ends with someone else wielding a brand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:05.520
new Black Panther suit, which is decked out&nbsp;
in gold details this time around. There are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.000
plenty of candidates out there, but it looks&nbsp;
like it might be Shuri getting some new duds.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.774
"Do not tell me what is&nbsp;
possible! Tell me the truth!"

00:02:12.346 --> 00:02:15.600
One of the biggest questions fans have&nbsp;
about "Wakanda Forever" revolves around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.320
the identity of the next Black Panther.&nbsp;
After all, T'Challa leaves some very big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:23.580
shoes to fill as the nation's leader and a key&nbsp;
member of the Avengers. The easiest option is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:27.360
obviously Shuri since she gets her own Black&nbsp;
Panther costume in the comics, and British&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.320
star Letitia Wright is reprising her role as&nbsp;
the king's sister in the sequel. There's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:35.160
some controversy surrounding Wright throughout&nbsp;
the pandemic, as she previously retweeted some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.780
supposedly anti-vaccination opinions, which&nbsp;
was met with heavy backlash from some fans.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.480
The Hollywood Reporter would&nbsp;
later claim that the actress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.240
was making her anti-vax stance known&nbsp;
while working on the "Black Panther"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:49.080
sequel in Atlanta. Wright later refuted&nbsp;
these reports on Instagram, saying,

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.720
"I honestly assert that&nbsp;
this was completely untrue."

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:56.280
So it'll be interesting to see whether she does&nbsp;
get her own suit. Wright previously told Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.340
Girl Nerds that Shuri throws herself&nbsp;
into her work as a way of processing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:03.420
her grief for T'Challa, so expect to see&nbsp;
plenty of new technology. She explained,

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:07.140
"So there's so much new technology to look&nbsp;
forward to, and I think that's where her sweet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.280
spot is at the moment. Like, 'How do I process&nbsp;
this?' And she just throws all of her energy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.120
even more so, into technology. So, there's&nbsp;
a lot of cool new things to look out for."

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:19.740
Rumors swirled online that Mexican star&nbsp;
Tenoch Huerta would be joining the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.520
as Namor the Submariner. This wasn't&nbsp;
confirmed until San Diego Comic-Con&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.840
2022 when Kevin Feige brought the star&nbsp;
onstage during Marvel Studios' Hall H&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.280
presentation. Huerta was pretty enthusiastic&nbsp;
about joining the MCU, telling the audience,

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:36.780
"I'm so happy to be here. It's an honor. I want&nbsp;
to say something really fast about inclusion:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.860
Thanks to inclusion I am here. I wouldn't be&nbsp;
here without inclusion. And a lot of kids are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:44.880
there looking at us grinning at us because&nbsp;
we're here. [By the way] Namor is amazing!"

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:49.680
A listing for Hasbro's Namor figure also&nbsp;
revealed a surprising fact about his home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.060
because while he's from Atlantis in the comics,&nbsp;
Marvel Studios has renamed the underwater kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:57.540
to Talocan. This was later confirmed in&nbsp;
a press release about the "Black Panther:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.160
Wakanda Forever" prologue album from Ludwig&nbsp;
Goranson. It's largely because Marvel has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.180
worked in Mayan/Aztec culture into Namor's&nbsp;
people. This can be seen in his design,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.420
which is complete with winged ankles&nbsp;
and green trunks from the comics.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:14.340
Believe it or not, Namor is actually Marvel's&nbsp;
very first mutant in the comics, chronologically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.200
speaking. He's a combination of Atlantean DNA&nbsp;
and human DNA, which grants him the powers of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:24.240
Talocans while also maintaining a typically human&nbsp;
appearance. It's an impressive mix of genes, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.843
aside from breathing underwater, Namor can also&nbsp;
fly, which also leads back to his mutant makeup.

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:34.380
The MCU is quickly racking up many younger heroes&nbsp;
across Kevin Feige's grand superhero tapestry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:39.420
and there's another one on her way: Riri Williams,&nbsp;
played by Dominique Thorne. Williams is a genius&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:43.560
inventor and a relatively new character in the&nbsp;
comics, first arriving in "Invincible Iron Man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:48.900
Vol. 3" #7. She builds her own version of the Iron&nbsp;
Man armor and eventually suits up as her own hero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:52.860
Ironheart. Feige revealed that Ironheart&nbsp;
is getting her own TV show at the 2020&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.460
Disney Investor Day presentation, which&nbsp;
was incredibly exciting news in itself.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.980
"Sometimes you gotta run before you can walk."

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.480
But it wasn't until August 2021 that&nbsp;
Feige revealed to ComicBook.com that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.540
Thorne will also have a supporting&nbsp;
role in "Wakanda Forever," saying,

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.260
"We're shooting Black Panther: Wakanda Forever,&nbsp;
right now, and the character of Riri Williams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:13.500
you will meet in Black Panther&nbsp;
2 first. She started shooting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.660
I think, this week before her Ironheart series."

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:20.160
For the moment it's not clear how Williams gets&nbsp;
involved with the Wakandans, mainly because her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.000
comics origin starts when she's at college&nbsp;
at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:28.680
One of the most memorable supporting&nbsp;
characters in Wakanda is the formidable M'Baku,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:32.640
played by Winston Duke, the leader of the&nbsp;
Jabari tribe. They're the most traditional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:36.060
clan in the isolated nation because they've&nbsp;
turned away from the country's reliance on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.380
vibranium and advanced technology. Instead,&nbsp;
M'Baku and his tribe live high up in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:44.520
mountains — only descending to meet other groups&nbsp;
for occasions like T'Challa's ascension to King,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:48.600
where the leader challenged him for the title&nbsp;
of Black Panther. He winds up becoming one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.900
T'Challa's allies after Michael B.&nbsp;
Jordan's Killmonger usurps the hero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:55.440
even saving him from certain death after&nbsp;
he was thrown from the top of a cliff.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.860
It seems like M'Baku has brought&nbsp;
the Jabari into the 21st century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.720
as Duke previously told Screen Rant,

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:04.500
"I think the events of 'Infinity War' and&nbsp;
'Endgame' really showed that the Jabari are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.880
now full-fledged members of Wakanda. M'Baku was&nbsp;
a part of every single conflict; every event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:12.960
and I don't think they could really exist in&nbsp;
isolation anymore. They have open borders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.860
and we saw that M'Baku was really Wakandan.&nbsp;
His entire community has expanded."

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:19.800
It sounds like he'll be at the forefront&nbsp;
of a lot of action this time around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:22.020
as The Hollywood Reporter previously revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.380
Duke has negotiated a bigger salary&nbsp;
for an expanded role in the sequel.

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:30.600
2018's "Black Panther" was stacked with a&nbsp;
truly talented cast, including British star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:34.800
Daniel Kaluuya, who was previously nominated&nbsp;
for Best Actor at the Oscars for his role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.520
in Jordan Peele's "Get Out." He won Best&nbsp;
Supporting Actor for "Judas and the Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:41.940
Messiah." He appears in "Black Panther"&nbsp;
as T'Challa's confidant and best friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:45.660
W'Kabi, a member of the Border tribe&nbsp;
whose father was killed by Andy Serkis'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:49.020
Ulysses Klaue years before the events&nbsp;
of the film. This is part of the reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.920
that he sides with Killmonger when he delivers&nbsp;
Klaue's body as a way of getting into Wakanda.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.040
Although W'Kabi's new alliance forced&nbsp;
him against his friends and family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.920
he manages to stay alive by&nbsp;
the end of the film. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:02.580
W'Kabi won't show up in "Wakanda Forever"&nbsp;
because Kaluuya was already set to work on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:06.420
Peele's science-fiction horror flick, "Nope."&nbsp;
According to Rotten Tomatoes' Jacqueline Coley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:10.620
the schedules for both films clashed at&nbsp;
the time. It's not surprising that Kaluuya&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:14.460
opted to stay onboard for "Nope," since he did&nbsp;
some of his best work with Peele in "Get Out."

00:07:14.445 --> 00:07:17.784
"It's in the cloud!"

00:07:17.784 --> 00:07:18.349
"Mhmm."

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:22.740
Marvel Studios has a great knack for&nbsp;
attracting Hollywood legends alongside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.460
up-and-coming talent — but "Black Panther:&nbsp;
Wakanda Forever" is a stacked cast full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:31.320
of huge names with years of experience behind&nbsp;
them. Angela Bassett is back as Queen Ramonda,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:36.660
while "The Walking Dead" alum Danai Gurira will&nbsp;
don her Dora Milaje uniform again as Okoye. She'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:40.560
be joined by Florence Kasumba's Ayo, who was&nbsp;
last seen in "The Falcon and The Winter Soldier."

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.760
"I May Destroy You" lead actress Michaela&nbsp;
Coel is joining the MCU as Aneka,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:48.180
who is a former member of the Dora&nbsp;
Milaje in the comics. Likewise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:52.680
Martin Freeman is back as CIA agent&nbsp;
Everett Ross. Meanwhile down in Talocan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:58.260
Tenoch Huerta's underwater forces are bolstered by&nbsp;
Mabel Cadena's Namora and Alex Livinelli's Attuma.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:02.100
The late Dorothy Steele has also reprised&nbsp;
her role as the Merchant Tribe leader in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:06.660
one of her final performances before her&nbsp;
death in October 2021 at the age of 95.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:11.520
Ryan Coogler is back on directing duties for&nbsp;
"Wakanda Forever." It's a complete no-brainer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:15.480
from Marvel Studios considering the first&nbsp;
film earned over $1 billion worldwide and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:19.080
was a critical hit as well as a commercial&nbsp;
one. Thankfully, the man behind "Fruitvale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:23.340
Station" and "Creed" isn't short of ideas for&nbsp;
the MCU, and he clearly works well within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:27.840
system alongside the likes of Kevin Feige and&nbsp;
Victoria Alonso. As per Forbes, the director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.520
signed on for the sequel back in 2018 — not long&nbsp;
after the first film raked in all that profit.

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:36.960
He's had a very difficult job of steering the&nbsp;
ship after Chadwick Boseman's untimely passing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:40.380
and it's not something he's taken lightly.&nbsp;
While speaking to The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:43.800
Coogler explained that he feels the star&nbsp;
would want him to carry on. He said,

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:48.300
"It's difficult. You've got to keep going when you&nbsp;
lose loved ones. I know Chad wouldn't have wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:52.380
us to stop. He was somebody who was so about the&nbsp;
collective [...] So it would be harder for me to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:56.160
stop. Truthfully. I'd feel him yelling at me,&nbsp;
like, 'What are you doing?' So you keep going."

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.020
"You've been warned."

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:01.440
Thankfully, the first teaser suggests&nbsp;
that Coogler has once again helmed an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.851
adventure that could be truly special.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:07.080
Let's face it, the MCU timeline is a&nbsp;
sprawling tapestry that is very hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:11.040
to keep track of. This is especially true when&nbsp;
you consider all the time-travel shenanigans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.600
that the Avengers and Loki get up to in the&nbsp;
movies and shows on Disney+. All of that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:19.200
only going to get more complicated as the&nbsp;
studio jumps head-first into the multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:23.400
with future projects like "Loki" Season 2,&nbsp;
"Avengers: The Kang Dynasty," and "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:27.360
Secret Wars." Thankfully, "Black Panther:&nbsp;
Wakanda Forever" seems to be more of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:31.080
a grounded movie rather than involving&nbsp;
cosmic concepts and alternate realities.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.460
Because it's also the final film of Phase 4, it&nbsp;
seems likely that it's set in the present day of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:39.840
the MCU, after the likes of "Ms. Marvel," "Thor:&nbsp;
Love and Thunder," and "She-Hulk." Although,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:43.860
considering it's introducing Namor to the big&nbsp;
screen for the very first time we can probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:48.720
expect to see some flashbacks to his origin and&nbsp;
how Talocan became the sunken city that it is now.

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:52.080
This isn't to say that it won't lead&nbsp;
up to bigger plot points and movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:55.320
But it seems like a safe bet that it'll&nbsp;
be focused on the here and now because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.482
it'll honor the legacy of both&nbsp;
Chadwick Boseman and T'Challa.

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:03.300
Okay, let's address the Doctor Doom in the room.&nbsp;
With movies like "Fantastic Four" and "Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:06.780
Secret Wars" on the horizon, it doesn't&nbsp;
seem long until we can predict when and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:10.680
where legendary villain Doctor Doom finally&nbsp;
returns to the big screen. But there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:14.820
a few rumors online suggesting that a new&nbsp;
version of the Latverian bad guy is on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:19.560
way. It makes sense if Marvel Studios borrows&nbsp;
from Jonathan Hickman's 2015 event series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:23.580
"Secret Wars." One persistent rumor&nbsp;
says that Doctor Doom will be revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.400
in some capacity towards the end of&nbsp;
"Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:31.140
A report from Bleeding Cool claims that Doom&nbsp;
puppeteers the war between Wakanda and Talocan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:36.060
for his own ends, although it's not clear why. The&nbsp;
site noted that while Doom's apparent role won't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:40.320
be big, it will imply that this Wakanda-Atlantis&nbsp;
war was a result of Doom's interference.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:45.660
Interesting. He's one of many villains who's&nbsp;
tried to overthrow Wakanda for many years, so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:49.740
it would hardly be surprising if he's just looking&nbsp;
to get his metal gauntlets on all that vibranium.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:54.180
It would be easy to imagine Doom taking his&nbsp;
rightful place in the MCU. But to introduce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:57.780
him solely as an overarching character&nbsp;
could be disappointing — unless he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:01.380
going to start showing up more frequently&nbsp;
over the next few years. We'll just have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:04.080
to endure the pain of waiting and&nbsp;
see whether Doctor Doom is coming.

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:07.920
"Painful? You don't know the meaning of the word."

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.440
When it comes to the Marvel Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.920
one can always expect a cameo or&nbsp;
two. Bridging heroes from one film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:18.240
to another is the backbone of how this comic&nbsp;
book-inspired universe handles itself. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:22.380
with the roster of the MCU franchise constantly&nbsp;
expanding, it has become more difficult to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:26.640
guess which characters might appear in which&nbsp;
movies. Aside from the confirmed cast list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:30.780
there are some knowledgeable guesses as to who&nbsp;
may pop up in "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:36.240
As confirmed at San Diego Comic-Con 2022, "Black&nbsp;
Panther: Wakanda Forever" will be the official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:40.500
end of Marvel's fourth phase. The exception&nbsp;
of course, as James Gunn stated on Twitter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:44.940
is that of "The Guardians of the Galaxy Holiday&nbsp;
Special," which will serve as an epilogue. Looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:48.360
back at Marvel's latest stories, one character&nbsp;
has helped to thread the phase together:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:52.740
the Sorcerer Supreme, Wong. He snuck his&nbsp;
way into multiple Phase Four outings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:56.520
including "Shang-Chi and the Legend of the&nbsp;
Ten Rings," "Spider-Man: No Way Home," and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:00.420
"She-Hulk." It would not be unexpected to see&nbsp;
the master sorcerer make another appearance.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:03.900
Meanwhile, another name that has been&nbsp;
closely linked to "Black Panther 2" is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:07.500
the MCU's newest Captain America,&nbsp;
Anthony Mackie. Despite the actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:10.680
stating that he is not in the film, he&nbsp;
did confirm that he visited the set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:14.880
via the Twitter account Black Panther News.&nbsp;
This led to speculation that this may be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.880 --> 00:12:18.660
the first time audiences see Mackie in his new&nbsp;
uniform since "Falcon and the Winter Soldier."

00:12:18.660 --> 00:12:21.120
Of course, the tragic fact is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:26.100
the upcoming "Black Panther" sequel is missing its&nbsp;
star, Chadwick Boseman. The character of T'Challa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:30.180
quickly became a fan favorite with his debut&nbsp;
in "Captain America: Civil War." Aside from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:34.560
headlining his own feature in 2018, Boseman&nbsp;
continued his reign as the king of Wakanda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:39.420
throughout two "Avengers" movies. Sadly, at&nbsp;
43 years old, Boseman died of colon cancer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.420 --> 00:12:44.460
in August 2020. Losing such an integral piece of&nbsp;
the franchise was undoubtedly difficult for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:49.260
cast and crew in moving forward with a sequel.&nbsp;
However, Chadwick's brother Derrick Boseman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:53.160
confirmed to TMZ that the late actor would have&nbsp;
wanted the legacy of "Black Panther" to continue.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:58.380
Though talks about recasting briefly swirled, they&nbsp;
were put to rest by Marvel Studios president Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:02.820
Feige, who confirmed that bringing in a new face&nbsp;
to play T'Challa was never an option. Further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:06.360
Feige told Deadline in 2021 that the&nbsp;
actor would not be inserted into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:10.380
movie through CGI. Most fans can agree that&nbsp;
Marvel made the right decision in proceeding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:14.400
with a sequel that honors Boseman rather than&nbsp;
replacing or simulating him. But that doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:18.480
change the fact that for the cast and crew,&nbsp;
there's a notable absence. Martin Freeman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:22.080
who will reprise his role as CIA&nbsp;
Agent Everett Ross, told Collider,

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.960
"At the heart of it, there's&nbsp;
quite a gap now, and you felt it."

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:29.400
Based on Freeman's remarks, audiences can expect&nbsp;
Boseman's presence to be felt throughout the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:32.272
especially as the plot centers&nbsp;
around his character's legacy.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:35.760
With the premiere of "Black Panther:&nbsp;
Wakanda Forever" fast approaching,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:39.120
fans began receiving their first clues&nbsp;
to the plot and premise of the sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:43.080
in 2022. The official synopsis&nbsp;
released by Marvel Studios reads:

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:48.480
"Queen Ramonda, Shuri, M'Baku, Okoye, and the&nbsp;
Dora Milaje fight to protect their nation from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:52.440
intervening world powers in the wake of&nbsp;
King T'Challa's death. As the Wakandans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:55.560
strive to embrace their next chapter, the&nbsp;
heroes must band together with the help of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:59.640
War Dog Nakia and Everett Ross and forge&nbsp;
a new path for the kingdom of Wakanda."

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:03.720
At the conclusion of the first "Black Panther"&nbsp;
movie, the King of Wakanda chose to reveal the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:07.200
secret nation to the world and share their&nbsp;
advancements with the rest of society.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:11.460
"We must find a way to look after one another."

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:16.140
The aftermath and revelations of this reveal&nbsp;
will significantly impact the sequel's plot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:20.040
especially as the nation of Wakanda is&nbsp;
left leaderless. It's also easy to guess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:23.220
that a new Black Panther will be crowned&nbsp;
during the events of "Wakanda Forever."

